        '_USER_MESSAGE_CLIP = 600\n_USER_MESSAGES_MAX = 40\n_TRIM_FRACTION = 0.10\n# What one attachment costs the model, for the estimate ONLY (the real number comes back\n# in provider usage). An image is priced at a vision ceiling rather than at the length of\n# its base64: Anthropic tops out near 1,600 tokens for a full-size image, and the tiling\n# schemes of the other vendors land in the same order. A PDF page is about an image, and\n# a few pages is the common case.\nIMAGE_TOKENS = 1_600\nFILE_TOKENS = 5_000\n# Reference images carried across the boundary with the compacted block. A picture the\n# user attached to be read, redrawn or checked is the task itself — summarizing it to the\n# word "[image]" ends the job. Bounded so the block cannot reclaim the window it freed.\nCARRY_IMAGES = 2\n\n\n# -- token math ---------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _part_chars(part: Any) -> int:\n    """Serialized length of ONE content part, with attachment payloads priced at what\n    the model is actually billed instead of at the length of their base64.\n\n    A `data:` URL is transport, not text: a 1.1 MB screenshot is ~1.47 M base64 chars,\n    which chars/4 reads as ~367 k tokens, while every vision provider prices that image\n    at a four-figure token count (Anthropic caps a full-size image at ~1,600; the tiling\n    schemes of the others land in the same order). Counting the payload made a brand-new\n    conversation carrying one screenshot read as 3.6x over the compaction trigger, so the\n    first turn compacted itself and the model lost the very image it was asked to redraw.\n    """\n    if not isinstance(part, dict):\n        return len(str(part))\n    kind = part.get("type")\n    if kind == "image_url":\n        url = (part.get("image_url") or {}).get("url")\n        if isinstance(url, str) and url.startswith("data:"):\n            return IMAGE_TOKENS * 4\n    elif kind == "file":\n        data = (part.get("file") or {}).get("file_data")\n        if isinstance(data, str) and data.startswith("data:"):\n            return FILE_TOKENS * 4\n    try:\n        return len(json.dumps(part, default=str))\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        return len(str(part))\n\n\ndef estimate_tokens(messages: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> int:\n    """chars/4 over the serialized messages — the fallback signal for providers that\n    never report usage (documented in the metering code). Attachment payloads are priced\n    per `_part_chars`, never by the length of their base64."""\n    total = 0\n    for msg in messages:\n        content = msg.get("content") if isinstance(msg, dict) else None\n        if isinstance(content, list):\n            rest = {k: v for k, v in msg.items() if k != "content"}\n            try:\n                total += len(json.dumps(rest, default=str))\n            except (TypeError, ValueError):\n                total += len(str(rest))\n            total += sum(_part_chars(part) for part in content)\n            continue\n        try:\n            total += len(json.dumps(msg, default=str))\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n',
